Adopt the ihbench section scheme and a gentler opening

Sections are now What is Instruct-FD?, Scoring, Results and Pipeline,
with Pipeline last, following the ihbench blog. Numbered kickers are
gone, since ihbench has none; that also retires the 01-07 numbering
that no longer matched the poster.

The opener becomes the question itself and leads with the concrete
decision a voice agent makes many times a minute, then the two things
that have to go right, then what existing full-duplex benchmarks
measure and what Instruct-FD measures instead.

Scoring is a new section: paired pass rate as the headline, and
per-instruction as the looser measure, with the gap between them named
as the informative part.

Results absorbs the leaderboard, the full configuration table, the
analysis figures and the failure transcripts as h3 subsections, the way
ihbench nests its findings under one heading.

